QuestGuidance.Register("en",401,{
[12801]="700494B8\n1\tTalk to Párgrub\tYou should talk to Párgrub.\n2\tTalk to Párgrub\tPárgrub can be found near Thorzhaf. You should speak with Párgrub about the match.\n",
[12802]="700494B4\n1\tTalk to Párgrub\tYou should talk to Párgrub.\n2\tTalk to Párgrub\tPárgrub can be found near Thorzhaf. You should speak with Párgrub about the match.\n",
[12803]="700190F6\n1\tSpeak with Hasta\tHasta is in the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works of Moria. You should speak with Hasta to find out what he will need to prepare a lure for the creature behind the disturbing rumours.\n",
[12804]="70071615\n1\tReturn to Ahâba\tYou have secured an alliance with the former thralls of Esh Mêkag and the Servants of Aradûn. You should return to Mizâdi in Ahâba.\n2\tComplete 'Instance: The Plan of Attack'\tMizâdi is ready to plan the attack of Emax Dûl with her assembled allies. You should talk to Mizâdi and complete 'Instance: The Plan of Attack'.\n3\tTalk to Mizâdi\tYou have fended off an attack on Ahâba and have, perhaps, met a new key ally. You should talk to Mizâdi.\n",
[12805]="700571B6\n1\tTalk to Vaskorn in Limlók\tVaskorn can be found at Limlók in the Floodfells. You should talk to Vaskorn.\n2\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard can be found in Limlók. You should talk to Runerik Knotbeard.\n",
[12806]="70053E6E\n1\tRetrieve the urn from Shakam Moz\tThe urn Rauniel seeks can be found at Shakam Moz in the hills of eastern Rath Dúath. You should retrieve the urn for Rauniel.\n2\tPour water into a vessel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur\tThe final vessel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath. You should pour water into the vessel for Rauniel.\n3\tTalk to Rauniel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur\tRauniel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath. You should talk to Rauniel.\n",
[12807]="7004DA37\n1\tCure poisoned birds (total: 2)\030Cure poisoned frogs (total: 2)\030Cure poisoned rabbits (total: 3)\030Cure poisoned squirrels (total: 3)\030Cure poisoned foxes (total: 2)\tPoisoned animals can be found north of the path in Eryn Lasgalen. You should cure animals poisoned by the Taurogrim.\n2\tComplete\tCompleted.\n",
[12808]="7007177F\n1\tTalk to the guard\tFaeron suggested talking to these people to learn more about them. You should talk to the guard at Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru.\n2\tTalk to Nabatínu\tThe guard has directed you to speak with his leader, Nabatínu, inside Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru.\n3\tTalk to Faeron\tNabatínu, who leads the people inside Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru, has identified himself as an enemy of Ordâkh, and recommends against going any further west into An Shêru. You should talk to Faeron about what Nabatínu has said.\n4\tTalk to Nabatínu\tFaeron has asked Nabatínu, leader of the people inside Gadim-ûn in north-eastern An Shêru, if he knows of any areas of blight in An Shêru. You should talk to Nabatínu to hear his answer.\n5\tTalk to Faeron\tNabatínu has told you that he and the others here were once thralls of the Ordâkhai and have now found their freedom. They work to free the others still bound in thralldom. You should discuss the situation with Faeron.\n6\tTalk to Rhadrog at his camp\tFaeron has offered to assist the Jatsakóri and will meet you back at the Rangers' camp south of Gadim-ûn. You should go to the Ranger camp and talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[12809]="7000001B\n1\tTalk to Wilcome Tunnelly\tWilcome Tunnelly is in Scary, east of Brockenborings. The Plough and Stars Inn is in Brockenborings, west of Scary. Halson Tubwort of The Plough and Stars has sent you down to Scary to fetch a shipment of gypsum that has gone astray.\n2\tBring the gypsum to Halson Tubwort\030Collect the powdered gypsum\tThe goblins who stole the gypsum cart came from the Scrag-dells north of Brockenborings. It seems that goblins have the gypsum intended for The Plough and Stars, you should travel to their camp and search for the missing cart.\n",
[12810]="700033DB\n1\tBring the treasure boxes to Áskell\030Collect treasure-boxes (total: 6)\tThe treasure boxes are kept in the river port of Kheledûl, east of Gondamon. Áskell has devised a new plan to punish the Dourhands for Gellir's death. He has asked you to raid the port-town of Kheledûl and recover boxes of treasure stolen from the Longbeards by the Dourhands.\n",
[12811]="70066770\n1\tDefeat Corsairs of Umbar in Tarlang's Crown (0/14) Defeat Gondorian freebooters (0/6)\tCorsairs and Gondorian freebooters can be found at Azruthor's Rue and throughout Tarlang's Crown. While exploring the ruined remains of Azruthor's encampment in Tarlang's Crown, you have encountered a number of Gondorian freebooters and Corsairs of Umbar. You should defeat them and make safe the road through Tarlang's Crown.\n2\tDefeat Corsairs of Umbar in Tarlang's Crown (total: 14)\030Defeat Gondorian freebooters (total: 6)\tCorsairs and Gondorian freebooters can be found at Azruthor's Rue and throughout Tarlang's Crown. While exploring the ruined remains of Azruthor's encampment in Tarlang's Crown, you have encountered a number of Gondorian freebooters and Corsairs of Umbar. You should defeat them and make safe the road through Tarlang's Crown.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Corsairs of Umbar and Gondorian freebooters in Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[12812]="7002CA8C\n1\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should bring the items to Idmar.\n2\tTalk to Doron\tDoron is among his men on the crest of the hill in western Parth Celebrant. Idmar wants you to speak with Doron regarding the Easterling.\n",
[12813]="70043025\n1\tFeed Spearflower to one of the goats in Imloth Melui\tThe goats can be found north-east of the Hall of the Gentle Hand, at the bottom of the long stairs. Brunil has asked you to feed each ingredient in the healing draught to a goat, one after another.\n2\tFeed Dusk-flower to one of the goats in Imloth Melui\tThe goats can be found north-east of the Hall of the Gentle Hand, at the bottom of the long stairs. Brunil has asked you to feed each ingredient in the healing draught to a goat, one after another.\n3\tFeed Maresfoot to one of the goats in Imloth Melui\tThe goats can be found north-east of the Hall of the Gentle Hand, at the bottom of the long stairs. Brunil has asked you to feed each ingredient in the healing draught to a goat, one after another.\n4\tTalk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tBrunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui. You fed all the ingredients in the draught to the goats, and the Maresfoot seemed to be disagreeable. You should return to Brunil with what you have learned.\n",
[12814]="70043026\n1\tCollect Dewleaf south-west of Imloth Melui (total: 6)\tDewleaf can be found on the bluff above River Erui, south-west of the entrance to Imloth Melui. Brunil has asked you to fetch as much Dewleaf as you can in order to counteract the poison her patients consumed.\n2\tReturn to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tBrunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui. You have collected as much Dewleaf as you could find, and should bring it to Brunil.\n3\tAdd the Dewleaf to the cure at the healer's workbench in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tThe healer's workbench is right by Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand. It is where she makes all of her medicines. Brunil has prepared the cure, and it will be complete once you add the Dewleaf. The cure waits for you on the healer's workbench.\n4\tThe poisoned patients can be found throughout the Hall of the Gentle Hand in Imloth Melui. You should administer the compounded cure to the patients who drank the poison.\t\n5\tTalk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tBrunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, in Imloth Melui. You should tell Brunil that the cure has been administered to all the poisoned patients.\n6\tTalk to Merenir in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tMerenir has come to the Hall of the Gentle Hand with a troubling report.\n",
[12815]="700479DE\n1\tEnter the enemy encampment of Dûm Boha\tThe Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills. You should collect phials of poison from Haradrim archers.\n2\tCollect phials of poison (total: 10)\tThe Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills. You should collect phials of poison from Haradrim archers.\n3\tReturn to Gladhir\tYou should return to Gladhir, who can be found at Haerondir.\n",
[12816]="700107C5\n1\tCatch as many fish as you can in twenty minutes.\tThe fish pond is east of Andrath farm. Will Hindmarsh has asked you to catch fish for the hobbits' Lithe Festival.\n",
[12817]="70065B68\n1\tCollect building materials (total: 8)\tHimril has asked you to travel to Arnach to the south and search for building materials.\n2\tTalk to Himril\tAll of these building materials should account for what is missing from Himril's records. You should return to Himril. Himril is in Imloth Melui.\n",
[12818]="7002731F\n1\tFind and challenge Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod\tYevan, Olwen, and Wundod can be found in Tûr Morva. Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the youthful fighters of the Falcon-clan in combat.\n2\tTalk to Mair in Tûr Morva\tMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras. You have easily defeated a youthful fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.\n3\tFind and challenge Sors, Eiviona, or Owein\tSors, Eiviona, and Owein can be found somewhere in Tûr Morva. Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the more accomplished fighters of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva.\n4\tTalk to Mair in Tûr Morva\tMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras. You have defeated an experienced fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.\n",
[12819]="7002C6F5\n1\tDefeat Celebrant brigands (total: 8)\030Defeat Celebrant relic-thieves (total: 4)\030Defeat Celebrant archers (total: 6)\tThe brigands have gathered to the south inside of a large camp known as Hordfierd. Doron has asked you to defeat many of the brigands which have invaded Parth Celebrant.\n2\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. Doron sent you to speak with Idmar, following your attack upon the brigands.\n",
[12820]="70054884\n1\tYou are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.\t\n2\tBreak fallen rubble (total: 8)\tFallen rubble can be found throughout the dungeons of Barad-dûr.\n",
[12821]="70053E6F\n1\tDefeat enemies outside Eithel Gwaur (total: 4)\030Reach the door to Eithel Gwaur\tEithel Gwaur can be found in eastern Rath Dúath. You should defeat enemies outside Eithel Gwaur.\n2\tRauniel remains trapped inside Eithel Gwaur. You should find Rauniel inside Eithel Gwaur and save her.\t\n3\tTalk to Arodor at Echad Uial\tArodor can be found at Echad Uial in Rath Dúath. You should talk to Arodor.\n",
[12822]="7006B773\n1\tTalk to Amâsu\tGirhâzi has asked you to speak to Amâsu about the prisoner.\n2\tFind where the prisoner is held\tAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. She has asked you to talk to the prisoner in the cell on the west side of the lodge and see what you can learn.\n3\tTalk to Khûldim Umûn\tAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. She has asked you to talk to the prisoner in the cell on the west side of the lodge and see what you can learn.\n4\tTalk to Girhâzi\tAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. You have talked to the prisoner and should now return to Girhâzi.\n",
[12823]="7002F9A0\n1\tEnter the Nink-hai camp and locate their leader\tExplore the Nink-hai camp along the mountain path east of Faldham. Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and overthrow the leader of the tribe.\n2\tUse the horn to draw Dargum's attention and defeat Grazadh\tThe Nink-hai leader can be found at the end of the mountain pass in the mountains. Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and defeat the leader of the tribe.\n3\tReturn to Langfrith and inform him of Dargum's escape\tLangfrith awaits oustide the mead hall of Faldham. Langfrith will wish to know of the events that transpired when you confronted the Nink-hai leader.\n",
[12824]="70015E4A\n1\tSave Anurandir\tBring Anurandir to safety.\n2\tTalk to Dornhador\tReturn to Dornhador in Echad Eregion. Inform Dornhador that you rescued Anurandir.\n",
[12825]="700664DD\n1\tTalk to Dravron\tDervorin wants to know why lumber production is so slow. Talk to Dravron about why his camp is not putting out lumber.\n2\tTalk to Dervorin\tDravron mentioned that his leadership of the camp stems from a land claim passed down through his family. Report this finding to Dervorin in Ethring.\n",
[12826]="70052433\n1\tEdlothon has asked you to speak with the hobbits of Woodhall in an effort to learn if the legendary Anarlossë somehow survived the decline of the Northern Kingdom.\t\n2\tTalk to Edlothon in the village of Woodhall\tEdlothon has come with you to the hobbit village of Woodhall, where you found some evidence of a flower resembling the legendary Anarlossë.\n3\tTalk to Marjoram Woolgather in the village of Woodhall\tMarjoram Woolgather wishes to speak with you and Edlothon.\n4\tFind the sun-flowers in the field to the north of Woodhall\tMarjoram Woolgather told you that sun-flowers border a farm-field north of Woodhall.\n5\tTalk to Edlothon in the field near Woodhall\tEdlothon stands by a row of sun-flowers in a field not far from the hobbit village of Woodhall.\n6\tTalk to Haerandel at the Festival Grounds\tHaerandel is at the Bree-land Festival Grounds.\n",
[12827]="7002C619\n1\tFind the prospector's shack\tYou should find the prospector's shack down in the Limlight Gorge.\n2\tTalk to Brid\tYou should speak with the remaining prospector from the expedition.\n",
[12828]="7002EDF2\n1\tAssist Offram with Blankets for the Winter\030Assist Offram with Horns for Battle\030Assist Offram with Making Meat-pies\tOffram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall at Eaworth. Offram has asked you to help provision the garrison and town of Eaworth.\n2\tTalk to Offram outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth\tOffram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth. You should return to Offram with news of your successes.\n",
[12829]="70000079\n1\tUse Moon\tThe vault is across Thorin's Hall to the north and up the stairs. Pull the vault levers in the right sequence. If you make a mistake, go back to Bávor Redstone to reset the gears. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tUse Axe\tThe vault is across Thorin's Hall to the north and up the stairs. Pull the vault levers in the right sequence. If you make a mistake, go back to Bávor Redstone to reset the gears. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tUse Sun\tThe vault is across Thorin's Hall to the north and up the stairs. Pull the vault levers in the right sequence. If you make a mistake, go back to Bávor Redstone to reset the gears. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tUse Jewel\tThe vault is across Thorin's Hall to the north and up the stairs. Pull the vault levers in the right sequence. If you make a mistake, go back to Bávor Redstone to reset the gears. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tBring the contents of the puzzle-vault to Bávor Redstone\030Collect the contents of the puzzle-vault\tBávor Redstone is back on the far side of Thorin's Hall to the south. Now that you have solved the riddle of the puzzle-vault, you should collect the treasure and bring it back to Bávor Redstone.\n",
[12830]="7000370B\n1\tTalk to Peg Pruner\tPeg Pruner is at the north end of the Archet town square. Constable Thistlewool mentioned that Peg Pruner may need assistance gathering food for the displaced inhabitants of Archet.\n",
[12831]="70044F27\n1\tMake your way through the Harlond with Aragorn\tMake your way through the Harlond with Aragorn's forces. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDefeat Kálmok and his squadron\tOpen the southern gate of the Rammas Echor so that Aragorn's men may make haste to the battle.\n3\tRegroup with Aragorn\tRegroup with Aragorn.\n4\tDefeat Orcs with Gimli and Halbarad\tDefeat Orcs with Gimli and Halbarad. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tHelp Legolas, Elladan, and Elrohir defeat a Mûmak\tHelp Legolas, Elladan, and Elrohir defeat a Mûmak. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver\tClear the Enemy off the of the blockaded bridge.\n",
[12832]="70044F26\n1\tMake your way through the Harlond with Aragorn\tMake your way through the Harlond with Aragorn's forces. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDefeat Kálmok and his squadron\tOpen the southern gate of the Rammas Echor so that Aragorn's men may make haste to the battle.\n3\tRegroup with Aragorn\tRegroup with Aragorn.\n4\tDefeat Orcs with Gimli and Halbarad\tDefeat Orcs with Gimli and Halbarad. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tHelp Legolas, Elladan, and Elrohir defeat a Mûmak\tHelp Legolas, Elladan, and Elrohir defeat a Mûmak. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver\tClear the Enemy off the of the blockaded bridge.\n",
})
